{"from": "text:acts-1-18-19", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-27-06-08-field-of-blood", "note": "Biblical cross-reference only (not evidence): Acts 1:18-19 gives a different account - Judas himself bought the field and fell headlong - against Matthew's priests buying the field and Judas hanging himself."}
{"from": "text:acts-1-18-19", "type": "related_to", "to": "person:judas-iscariot", "note": "Biblical cross-reference only: the different Acts account of Judas's death."}
{"from": "text:deuteronomy-21-6-7", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-27-24-25-pilate-washed-hands", "note": "Biblical cross-reference only (not evidence): the elders washing their hands over the heifer and disclaiming the blood (Deut 21:6-7) is the scriptural backdrop of Pilate's hand-washing; it is not outside evidence for the event."}
{"from": "text:psalm-22-18", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-27-35-garments-divided", "note": "Biblical cross-reference only (not evidence): Psalm 22:18 is the text Matthew echoes ('they divide my garments... cast lots'); it is a source of the wording, not independent evidence for the custom."}
{"from": "text:papias-expositions-judas", "type": "related_to", "to": "person:judas-iscariot", "note": "Reception (not evidence): Papias (c. 100-130 CE) hands on a different, legendary death of Judas - his body bloated and bursting on his own land - told in competition with Matthew and Acts; dependent on later Christian tradition."}
{"from": "text:papias-expositions-judas", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-27-03-05-judas-returned-silver", "note": "Reception (not evidence): Papias's Judas tradition differs from Matthew's account in every detail; recorded as an early Christian reception of the Judas story."}
{"from": "text:papias-expositions-judas", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-judas-papias"}
{"from": "text:mishnah-pesachim-8-6", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:sefaria-pesachim-8-6"}
{"from": "text:mishnah-pesachim-8-6", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-27-15-passover-release-custom", "grade": "D", "note": "Mishnah Pesachim 8:6 allows slaughtering the Passover for 'one whom the governing body promised to release from prison on the night of Passover' - a Passover prisoner-release practice in rabbinic memory; the Mishnah was compiled c. 200 CE, so it is later, not a contemporary record."}
{"from": "artifact:pilate-stone", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "A", "note": "The inscription names '[Po]ntius Pilatus, [praef]ectus Iuda[e]ae' - the person himself, with his office."}
{"from": "artifact:pilate-prutahs", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "B", "note": "Coins struck under his governorship 29/30-31/32 CE; they name Tiberius, not Pilate, so they fix the office and years rather than the name."}
{"from": "artifact:pilate-ring", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "D", "note": "A Herodium ring engraved 'Pilates'; the excavators state all explanations for the owner are equally possible - whether it is the prefect's own ring is disputed."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-18-55-64", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus narrates Pilate's governorship from appointment to his Jerusalem provocations - the same man and office."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-2-169-177", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "A", "note": "War 2.169-177 narrates Pilate's conduct as governor in Jerusalem - the man in the Passion setting."}
{"from": "text:philo-embassy-38-pilate", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "A", "note": "A contemporary names 'Pilate... appointed governor of Judaea' and describes his conduct in Jerusalem."}
{"from": "text:tacitus-annals-15-44", "type": "attests", "to": "person:pontius-pilate", "grade": "A", "note": "Tacitus names 'Pontius Pilatus' as the procurator who executed Christus under Tiberius - a Roman witness to the man."}
{"from": "text:acts-1-18-19", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:bible-api-acts-1-18-19"}
